{"id": "tea:brahma-samhita:5.1", "source": "src:brahma-samhita", "location": {"ref": "5.1"}, "paraphrase": "Kṛṣṇa, called Govinda, is the supreme Lord; his form is being, consciousness and bliss; he is without beginning, the beginning of all, the cause of all causes.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "original": {"text": "īśvaraḥ paramaḥ kṛṣṇaḥ sac-cid-ānanda-vigrahaḥ | anādir ādir govindaḥ sarva-kāraṇa-kāraṇam ||", "script": "IAST", "edition": "recalled from the standard text (skeleton); verify in Phase D", "licence": "public domain (pre-modern text)"}, "concepts": ["cpt:krsna-svayam-bhagavan"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:brahma-samhita:5.29", "source": "src:brahma-samhita", "location": {"ref": "5.29"}, "paraphrase": "I worship Govinda, the primeval person, tending the wish-fulfilling cows in abodes of wish-fulfilling gems surrounded by wish-fulfilling trees, served with reverence by hundreds of thousands of goddesses of fortune.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "meditation"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "world-fate"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "concepts": ["cpt:spiritual-abode"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:brahma-samhita:5.37", "source": "src:brahma-samhita", "location": {"ref": "5.37"}, "paraphrase": "Govinda, the soul of all, dwells in Goloka itself with those (gopīs) who are his own forms and potencies, imbued with rasa of bliss and consciousness.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "concepts": ["cpt:parakiya-svakiya", "cpt:radha-hladini-sakti"], "disputes": ["dsp:svakiya-parakiya"], "notes": "Jīva cites this verse ('nija-rūpatayā kalābhiḥ') for the gopīs' being his own potencies.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:brahma-samhita:5.38", "source": "src:brahma-samhita", "location": {"ref": "5.38"}, "paraphrase": "The saints, their eyes of devotion anointed with the salve of love, always see him within their hearts: Śyāmasundara, of inconceivable qualities.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["powers-experiences"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:brahma-samhita:5.40", "source": "src:brahma-samhita", "location": {"ref": "5.40"}, "paraphrase": "The undifferentiated, infinite, complete Brahman, differentiated into the glories of countless universes, is the effulgence of his body — I worship Govinda.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "concepts": ["cpt:brahman-paramatman-bhagavan"], "disputes": ["dsp:saguna-nirguna"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:brahma-samhita:5.48", "source": "src:brahma-samhita", "location": {"ref": "5.48"}, "paraphrase": "The lords of the universes, born from the pores of Mahāviṣṇu's body, live for the duration of one of his exhalations; that Mahāviṣṇu is a portion of a portion of Govinda.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "cosmic", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["world-fate"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "concepts": ["cpt:three-purusa-avataras"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
